@host = http://localhost:5104

### Health (no token needed)
GET {{host}}/health

### Register a customer (no token needed)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmet@example.com", "password": "Correct-Horse-9" }

### Sign in, then copy "accessToken" from the response into @token below. It expires after 15 minutes.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmet@example.com", "password": "Correct-Horse-9" }

###
@token = paste-the-access-token-here

### Who am I?
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refresh: paste "refreshToken" from the sign-in response. Send it twice: the second time is a reuse, and the
### session is over, including the token the first call returned.
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "paste-the-refresh-token-here" }

### Sign out
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "paste-the-refresh-token-here" }

### Without a token: 401
GET {{host}}/me

### Open an account (copy the "id" from the response into @ahmet / @ayse below).
### Send it twice: the same account comes back. Change the key for a second account.
POST {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: account-1

{ "currency": "TRY" }

###
@ahmet = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@ayse = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Sign in as the teller (SeedTeller in user-secrets, see the README), then paste the access token into @teller
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "teller@example.com", "password": "paste-the-teller-password-here" }

###
@teller = paste-the-teller-access-token-here

### A customer cannot pay in: 403
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{ahmet}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: deposit-forbidden

{ "amount": 100.00, "currency": "TRY" }

### Pay in 100 TL as the teller. Send it twice with the same key: the balance grows once. Change the key for a new deposit.
POST {{host}}/accounts/{{ahmet}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{teller}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: deposit-1

{ "amount": 100.00, "currency": "TRY" }

### Balance
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{ahmet}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My accounts
GET {{host}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### What happened on the account, newest first. To get the next page, paste "nextCursor" from the response into &after=
GET {{host}}/accounts/{{ahmet}}/entries?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Transfer 30 TL. Send it twice: the second answer is the first one replayed (Idempotent-Replayed: true).
### Change the key for a new transfer. Copy the "id", or "transferId" from a 422, into @transfer below.
POST {{host}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-1

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{ahmet}}", "destinationAccountId": "{{ayse}}", "amount": 30.00, "currency": "TRY" }

### Same key, different amount: 422 idempotency.key_reused
POST {{host}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-1

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{ahmet}}", "destinationAccountId": "{{ayse}}", "amount": 31.00, "currency": "TRY" }

###
@transfer = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Transfer status
GET {{host}}/transfers/{{transfer}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
